# Normalize line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# Development happens on Windows; everything that consumes this repo — the
# Docker image, Render's container start command, GitHub Actions — is Linux. Without
# this, a file committed with CRLF reaches a container and fails in ways that
# read as anything but a line-ending problem: a shell script whose shebang has
# a trailing \r reports "no such file or directory" naming a binary that plainly
# exists, and a .env-style file yields values with an invisible \r appended.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text and store it as LF, while checking it
# out with the platform's convention. Nothing about the working copy changes.
* text=auto

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Recorded provider responses. Byte-for-byte fixtures: an SSE stream is framed
# by \n\n, and a checkout that rewrote those to \r\n\r\n would change what the
# parser is being tested against.
tests/fixtures/** -text
